[b]LibGamepadContextMenuBridge[/b]

Use inventory actions from compatible keyboard/mouse addons in ESO's gamepad item-action menu. The bridge works with addons that register these actions through LibCustomMenu.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Compatible inventory actions, with supported submenu entries shown as Parent: Child.
[*]Checkbox toggles within supported submenus.
[*]Mark and unmark eligible items as junk.
[*]Optional TTC prices, vendor value and item-status information.
[*]Crafting material cost estimates. Missing prices are marked as incomplete; comparisons are not net profit.
[*]Separate account-wide settings for EU and NA.
[/list]

[b]Requirements and installation[/b]
[list]
[*]Required: LibCustomMenu 7.3.0 or newer (AddOnVersion 730 or newer).
[*]Optional: LibAddonMenu-2.0 for the settings panel.
[*]Optional: Tamriel Trade Centre and its price data for market prices and material cost estimates.
[/list]
Install these separately. Place the LibGamepadContextMenuBridge folder in ESO's live/AddOns directory, then enable it and LibCustomMenu in the addon list.

With LibAddonMenu: Settings > Addon Settings > LibGamepadContextMenuBridge.
Without it: /lgcmb on or /lgcmb off. Use /lgcmb status to check the current state.

[b]Compatibility and test status[/b]
For the desktop client, targeting ESO API 101051. Console support is not claimed.

Submenu entries appear as flat actions, not nested menus. Headers, dividers and disabled actions are omitted. Some mouse-only actions are not supported: clicks on submenu titles, top-level checkboxes and dynamically built submenu entries. The bridge does not convert arbitrary keyboard interfaces.

[b]1.5.5 is a beta build. It has been tested locally, but still needs testing in ESO.[/b] Compatibility with every LibCustomMenu addon is not guaranteed.

For a problem report, include the bridge and affected addon versions, the item/menu involved, and the steps to reproduce it. Remove private information from screenshots.

